{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790283279,"nonce":"AoENAlkf8qAH2x1OdTKBwlxlDU8=","message":"Revised 2026-09-24 (Luis), the full decision, superseding comment #5 the same day. Design: doc/design/terminal-renderer.md.\n\nNo `tui` command: the renderer sits behind `git work view KIND [KWARGS] [--gui]` and behind `git work flow run` whenever the flow calls `work.view.*`. Framework is Bubble Tea v2 (charm.land/bubbletea/v2, bubbles/v2, lipgloss/v2), Go only. gocui termui and gocui itself are deleted by the migration (bf6f392), not before, because the list renderer must exist before termui becomes useless.\n\nThe command is the spec. A view's input is one KWARGS object, the same object work.view.KIND(**kwargs) takes; nothing is read from stdin and nothing is printed, because the input already is the serialization. `Spec` and `IsSpec` leave package view; `git work view` has no --format; flow run keeps --format for what the flow returns. --gui posts the same object to the gui process (8b06191) and errors until it exists; no TTY and no --gui is an error too. An agent that wants data runs `git work issue PROGRAM`.\n\nA view call blocks on the script's thread and returns the user's answer (None for every kind today). Internally the Bubble Tea event loop runs on its own goroutine and the blocked script goroutine is a worker taking queued work, so navigation and redraw never wait on a script and a second edit queues behind a running one. The layout is built now, its clients later.\n\nArguments, three tiers (required / defaulted / feature). `query` is on every kind, defaulting to the list's default program. list: defaulted fields ([\"title\"]; the id is always first and unnamed); features details, group_by, expand, depth, rank. board: required columns; defaulted values (schema order), card ([\"title\"]); features group_by (swimlanes), rank — a value not in `values` gets a trailing column so nothing vanishes. gantt: required start and stop; defaulted label (title), scale (day|week|month|quarter, default week), from, to (the data's extent); features progress, group_by, expand, depth, rank. show: required id; defaulted fields (the type's fields in schema order). sort_by and card_title are gone — order is the query's order; gantt's `end` is renamed `stop`.\n\nNavigation reads arrows, vim and emacs at once: up up/k/C-p, down down/j/C-n, left left/h/C-b, right right/l/C-f, page PgUp,PgDn / C-u,C-d / M-v,C-v, ends Home,End / g,G / M-\u003c,M-\u003e. list up/down = items at the current nesting depth, left/right = between the editable `fields` columns; board up/down within a column, left/right between columns; gantt up/down between rows, left/right between time periods, the cursor a cell and the window scrolling to keep it visible. Nesting keys when built: Tab into the first child, Shift-Tab to the parent, z fold/unfold.\n\nGrab replaces every drag binding: Space grabs the item under the cursor (border blinks), direction keys move it, Space or Enter drops it, Esc puts it back; one drop is one commit however many moves. list grabbed: up/down change rank within group and level. board grabbed: left/right set the `columns` field to the neighbouring value, up/down change rank. gantt grabbed: left/right shift by one period of the current scale — on the bar's first cell only start moves, on its last cell only stop, in between both; up/down change rank. Reparenting a grabbed list item (writing the `expand` relation) is out of the first cut.\n\nSame on every kind: Enter opens show for the issue under the cursor and Esc returns to the view where it was; `e` edits the field under the cursor in place, or asks which field on a card or a bar, the widget chosen by the schema kind (value list for enum, toggle for bool, input line for text/number/date, identity list for identity; relations later); `c` adds a comment; `y` yanks the id over OSC 52; `/` narrows the visible rows by text locally, never a write; `?` lists the keys; `q` quits. show adds `t` to switch between comments and the full op log. Every write goes through package host; a refusal (schema check included) shows in the status line and nothing moves.\n\nRefresh: the view runs its own query, re-runs it when the ref watcher (63c68d1) reports a change and after each of its own writes, keeping the cursor on the same id. No provider function and no static list — both were artefacts of the earlier E9 text, not decisions. jq is enough because it is the program `git work issue` takes and `.` is the whole array; what is given up is rows that are not issues.\n\nRank: the `rank` binding (a field of kind rank, 441dcbb) changes the order rule — within each group, column or nesting level the view sorts by (rank, id), issues without a rank last, and the query then only selects. Without `rank` the query's order stands and grabbing moves nothing vertically. A drop writes one midpoint key to one issue.\n\nNesting is designed now and built after the migration: `expand` names a relation field, `depth` how far (default 1, unlimited allowed, cycles cut). The query selects the roots; a matched issue that is another matched issue's child shows nested once; a child the query did not match still shows under its parent. Every level uses the same fields, details, group_by. Gantt nests as rows under rows, not blocks within a row, which would overlap; a folded parent draws its own bar, or its children's envelope when it has no dates.\n\nDeferred together, not decided: actions injected into views (actions={\"Start\": start_fn} as buttons on rows, cards and show plus a global bar), which subsumes the on_change/on_select callback sketch of comment #5; work.view.split; questions to the user (choose/confirm/ask/form); reparenting by grab. pick=True is removed, not deferred: `flow pick ID` (9a24c8e) takes its id from the command line.\n\nConcurrency: the renderer holds no lock while open; reads never lock and each write takes the short write lock (d35de2e). The watcher starts when a view opens and stops when it closes.\n\nSequence: (1) list and show MVP without nesting, tested on scratch repos, being built now; (2) the migration bf6f392, which deletes entities/bug, commands/bug, termui and gocui; (3) board, then gantt, then nesting.","files":null}]}